WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:02.820
John: Good morning Hank; it's 5:48 in the
morning, the Paper Towns movie starts filming

00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:04.910
in like 1 hour and 12 minutes.

00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:08.590
I'm extremely excited and nervous, wait- I-
something looks different.

00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:10.670
Oh, I got new glasses, no that's not it.

00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:11.670
Oh!

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:12.670
It's the creepy moustache.

00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:14.260
I've been setting that joke up for more than
2 months.

00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:17.340
When I ordered my new glasses, they were like
"It's going to be 8 to 10 weeks" and I was

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:19.480
like "Perfect, I'll grow a beard."

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:23.050
Alright I have to shave I can't let the movie
people meet me like this, by the way relevant

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:24.050
T-shirt.

00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:25.270
Look Hank I have my own chair.

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:27.520
So Hank people keep asking me what an executive
producer does.

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:32.050
I don't know, I just listen to the headphones
and, uh, I get a chair with my name on it,

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:33.050
and I think that's it.

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:34.050
Nat: Hey guys.

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:35.850
John: Uh, so this is Nat Wolff who plays Q
in the movie.

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:36.850
We just started filming.

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:38.499
That's not weird, just keep doing that.

00:00:38.499 --> 00:00:42.190
It's great, thank you, thanks for being in
my video today.

00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:45.379
Okay this is like the only place I can film
outside without giving away our location.

00:00:45.379 --> 00:00:47.789
It's a nice brisk day here in North Carolina.

00:00:47.789 --> 00:00:49.260
Feels just like Orlando in April.

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:52.889
So Hank I was just literally jumping up and
down with Jaz Sinclair who plays Angela in

00:00:52.889 --> 00:00:57.460
the movie because this is all just like so
exciting and wonderful and amazing I can't

00:00:57.460 --> 00:00:58.840
-aaaaaaahhh!

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:01.449
I'm going to have to do my happy dance, but
I'm holding the camera so it's gonna look

00:01:01.449 --> 00:01:02.449
a little weird.

00:01:02.449 --> 00:01:07.250
Also there's like 40 people in the crew, you
know, who are going to watch this, but whatever

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:10.820
I'm so ha ha ha ha yiiiess!

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:12.479
How'd I look?

00:01:12.479 --> 00:01:13.479
Good?

00:01:13.479 --> 00:01:15.450
Alright I'm gonna go back inside Radar's house
now which is full of black Santas.

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:18.009
I wish I could show you the black Santas;
there are literally thousands.

00:01:18.009 --> 00:01:21.130
Hank there are so many things that amaze me
about movies, like the incredibly expensive

00:01:21.130 --> 00:01:26.270
cameras, but the thing I will never get over
is the quality of the port-a-potties, I mean

00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:30.119
look at this, is this a port-a-potty or a
mansion?

00:01:30.119 --> 00:01:31.960
For god's sakes it's got hard wood floors.

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:37.409
So Hank we've now left Radar's house and we
find ourselves by a pond.

00:01:37.409 --> 00:01:38.409
That's all I can tell you.

00:01:38.409 --> 00:01:41.399
I just wanted to quickly comment on your great
video about being a young person and not voting.

00:01:41.399 --> 00:01:43.890
When I was a young person, I did not vote
a lot.

00:01:43.890 --> 00:01:48.070
Like I missed several elections that in retrospect
were pretty important to American history,

00:01:48.070 --> 00:01:52.890
and I missed them because, well mostly because
I was like nervous and I didn't know how to

00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:53.890
vote.

00:01:53.890 --> 00:01:56.180
So I just wanted to say that anyone who's
like me and really nervous about, like, the

00:01:56.180 --> 00:02:01.409
prospect of voting for the first time, I understand
that it's a little bit scary, but once you

00:02:01.409 --> 00:02:02.819
do it, you're gonna feel awesome.

00:02:02.819 --> 00:02:07.390
Hank, if it looks a little darker that's because
it is a little darker because we just finished

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:10.030
day one, huzzah!

00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:12.180
Producer Wyck Godfrey how you feelin'?

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:13.220
Wyck: Huzzaah!

00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:15.320
John: That seems fake, but it's going well.

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:18.672
Hank I got back after the end of a long day
and look, look, I have a trailer!

00:02:18.672 --> 00:02:20.500
I have my own trailer!

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:22.860
It's got the fancy Hollywood lights.

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:26.240
Aww, man this couch is so comfortable, I love
being an executive producer.

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:29.920
I want to be an executive producer for every
movie, does the new Divergent movie need an

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:31.080
executive producer?

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:32.080
Because I am available.

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:37.240
Aww, that reminds me of how much I miss Shailene
and Ansel, but I am so, so excited about this.

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:40.220
Hank, one of the scenes we filmed today was
the first part of Paper Towns I ever wrote.

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:41.791
I wrote it like 9 years ago.

00:02:41.791 --> 00:02:47.030
And it was just so weird and wonderful to
see little Q and little Margo biking up to

00:02:47.030 --> 00:02:49.730
this, you know, dead body.

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:53.320
Sounds weird when I put it that way, but anyway
it was wonderful, I cried a little bit.

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:55.170
To be fair, I cry a lot on movie sets.

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:59.060
Crazy, crazy, crazy thanks to everybody involved
in the Paper Towns movie.

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:00.540
Hank, don't forget to vote!

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:04.030
Nerdfighters, in America who are over the
age of 18, don't forget to vote!

00:03:04.030 --> 00:03:05.030
And don't forget to be awesome.

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:05.980
I'll see you on Friday.

